 that I love that the  supporting cast was fantastic to  Jennifer Garner and Josh Duhamel not  only were they important because just  look at them you're like yeah you got  that put together house don't you have  white picket fence going on but the  important thing they bring to the table  is that in a world where it's a movie  about a kid coming out how do his  parents handle it how do his friends  handle it how do people handle it I  adored his friends but at one point I  just felt like they were overreacting a  bit over something I was like you guys  are kind of making this all about you  and you're kind of being Dexter right  now overreacting is the word I used in  my head then I just realized whoa  they're teenagers they're supposed to  overreact yeah any teenagers watching  this if your mom or your parent or an  adult is coming at you just be like I'm  a kid I'm supposed to overreact  I imagine any adult who hears a kid say  that will be like  probably self-aware yet one of those any  more than that it'll start to wear and  there's one character that hangs out  with them I didn't like him at all I  know you're not really supposed to love  him in the movie but I just felt like he  went so far it he he was a bit  unredeemable for me I get it was to  drive the plot forward and he did his  part for the plot movie didn't do a good  enough job at redeeming him if they ever  needed to redeem him special shout out  to the drama t-shirt we're talking scene  stealer any scene with the drama teacher  she's the only one you know she's  amazing she's fantastic again don't know  what I've seen her in because I'm [ __ ]  with phases apparently but I do want to  see her more stuff guys in the end love  Simon I truly loved loved Simon it's a  movie that's set out to do certain  things and I personally feel it  succeeded in although this is the best  coming-of-age story since age of 17 that  I've personally saying I haven't seen  all of them I get that but it's my  favorite sense this movie can and will  connect with anyone who has ever been  searching for love in their life  especially in high school it may connect  more with some people on a deeper and  personal level that's the beauty of  cinema but this movie's not walled off  to anybody it's a movie for everybody  and I will say love Simon is definitely  worth watching and definitely worth  buying on blu-ray  alright so love Simon have you seen it  what did you think about it I'm filming  this on Saturday so I don't know how  many people watch the movie at this  point hope a lot did what's your  favorite coming-of-age story whatever  you think comment below let me know and  as always if you like what you've seen  here and you want to see more click  right here to see more  [Music]

